s="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page nav-item nav-item-211"><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/uganda-car-rental-hire/" class="dropdown-item ">Uganda Car Rental &amp; Hire</a></li><li id="menu-item-208" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page nav-item nav-item-208"><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/support-local-communities/" class="dropdown-item ">Support Local Communities</a></li><li id="menu-item-238" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-post nav-item nav-item-238"><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/information/uganda-travel-tips/" class="dropdown-item ">Uganda Travel Tips</a></li><li id="menu-item-195" class="menu-item menu-item-type-taxonomy menu-item-object-category nav-item nav-item-195"><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/safari-news/" class="dropdown-item ">Travel blog</a></li></ul></li><li id="menu-item-206" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page nav-item nav-item-206"><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/contact-us/" class="nav-link ">Contact</a></li></ul> </div> </div> </nav> </header> <div class="banner-home w-100 position-relative" itemprop="image" style="min-height: 120vh;"> <div class="main-overlay position-absolute top-0 start-0 w-100 h-100 index-3"></div> <div class="home-banner-text position-absolute w-100 h-100 index-5"> <div class="container-fluid container-xl h-100"> <div class="row h-100"> <div class="col-12 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center content-wrapper"> <div class="text-shadow-main text-white mobile-padding"> <h1 class="pt-5 pt-sm-4 mb-3" itemprop="headline"><br>Welcome to<br><span class="big-text">Lake Bunyonyi Uganda - Lake Bunyonyi Tours &amp; Safaris</span></h1> <h4 class="mb-4 mb-sm-5">Lake Bunyonyi has <strong>29 islands and a lot of history</strong> in Kabale. Visit Lake Bunyonyi Uganda for spectacular scenery and viewing amazing community tours!!</h4> <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-lg-row justify-items-center gap-3 gap-sm-4 pt-2 pt-lg-3 pt-xl-5"> <a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/uganda-safaris-tours/" class="btn btn-lg btn-warning rounded-pill me-lg-4 px-5"> VIEW SAFARIS <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-arrow-right-short" viewBox="0 0 16 16"> <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M4 8a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h5.793L8.146 5.354a.5.5 0 1 1 .708-.708l3 3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .708l-3 3a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L10.293 8.5H4.5A.5.5 0 0 1 4 8z"></path> </svg> </a> <a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/uganda-tour-companies/" class="btn btn-lg btn-outline-light rounded-pill px-5"> CHOOSE A TOUR OPERATOR <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-arrow-right-short" viewBox="0 0 16 16"> <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M4 8a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h5.793L8.146 5.354a.5.5 0 1 1 .708-.708l3 3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .708l-3 3a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L13.293 8.5H1.5A.5.5 0 0 1 1 8z"></path> </svg> </a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div></div><div class="d-block d-sm-none" style="height: 20px;"></div> <main class="site-content"><section class="intro-section w-100 bg-lighter-brown-alt pb-5 py-sm-4"> <div class="container-fluid container-xl"> <div class="row"> <div class="intro-div position-relative index-5 col-lg-12 bg-white div-shadow-main radius-20 p-5 mt-0 align-self-start mb-5 mb-xl-0"> <div class="entry-header"> <h2 class="mb-5" itemprop="headline">Visit Lake Bunyonyi (The Place of Many Little Birds) in Kabale-Uganda</h2> </div> <div class="entry-content" itemprop="text"> <p><strong>Lake Bunyonyi Uganda</strong>, also called the Place of Many Little Birds, is located in south-western Uganda between the districts of Kisoro and Kabale, close to the border with Rwanda. Itâ€™s located at 1,962 m (6,437 ft) above sea level; it is about 25 km (15.5 mi) long and 7 km (1.35 mi) wide.</p><div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"><iframe style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;" data-src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/GOQsDoypaMs?end=198" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" src="cid:frame-943C2DCB1A560F629477246000AB5017@mhtml.blink" class="lazyload" data-load-mode="0"><br /></iframe></div><p>The <strong>depth of Lake Bunyonyi is expected to vary between 44 m (144 ft.)</strong> and 900 m (2,952 ft.), which, if true, would make the lake the second deepest in Africa. Rumor has it that it is one of the few lakes in the region free of bilharzia and safe for swimming.</p><p>Geographically, Lake Bunyonyi is a body of water seven kilometers or 4.3 miles west of Kabale Town, southwestern Uganda. It is 25 km long and 7 km (4.3 mi) wide, covering an area of 61 square kilometers (23Â½ sq. miles).</p><p><b>The altitude of Lake Bunyonyi is 1,950 meters above sea level, </b><strong>with hills ranging from 2,200 to 2,478 meters high and heavily cultivated surrounding it</strong>. The central part of the lake, home to 29 islands with few settlements, primarily hosts tourist facilities and secondary and primary school study tours.</p><p>The data on the lakeâ€™s maximum depth varies from 44 m to 900 m (144 to 2,952 ft) in parts. If the latter is accurate, Lake Bunyonyi stands as the second-deepest lake in Africa, a fact confirmed by <a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/uganda-safaris-tours/">Uganda safari</a> travelers who visit the lake during their <a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/safari-news/uganda-birding-safaris-in-lake-bunyonyi/">Uganda Birding safaris</a> or during their <a href="https://www.primeugandasafaris.com/">adventure vacation safari holiday tours in Uganda</a>, Rwanda, and Africa.</p><p>The <strong>Lake Bunyonyi</strong> <strong>temperature on the surface rises to 25 degrees Celsius (77 Â°F)</strong>. Later years saw the introduction of fish to the lake, leading to the profitability of fishing in the 1930s. Regrettably, in the 1960s, we anticipated wind-induced violent shallow mixing, which led to the mass death of fish.</p><p>People primarily used the lake for subsistence fishing, catching Clarias species. The depth and stratification of the lake pose challenges for the breeding of common Ugandan species such as Nile Perch and Tilapia. Nevertheless, the end of 2002 saw the release of 300,000 Nile Tilapias and Clarias fish into the lake. The lake also harbors mudfish, crayfish, and mirrowcarp, along with a multitude of their predators, including otter.</p><p>The towns on its shores include Kyevu and Muko, while its 29 islands include Punishment Island and Bushara Island. It is a popular location for watersports and is known for the surrounding terraced hillsides. It is popular with both foreign and domestic tourists and there is a wide variety of tourist accommodations.</p><p>Many tourists and travelers who undertake a gorilla trekking safari in Uganda or come to Uganda after their Rwanda gorilla safari experience rest and relax at the beautiful Lake Bunyonyi as they enjoy the best scenery in the whole world and involve themselves in various cultural and community activities as well as birding and canoe rides.</p><p>Two tribes, the Bakiga and the Batwa, live in Bufuka Village, the lakeâ€™s main center.</p><h2 style="text-align: center;">Below Are Top Uganda Safari Tours Featuring Lake Bunyonyi</h2> </div> <div class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start flex-md-row align-items-start align-content-md-center justify-content-md-between"> <div><a href="https://www.lakebunyonyiuganda.com/contact-us/" class="btn btn-lg btn-danger rounded-pill border-0 me-4 me-md-0 px-5 div-shadow-main"> START PLANNING NOW <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-arrow-right-short" viewBox="0 0 16 16"> <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M4 8a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h5.793L8.146 5.354a.5.5 0 1 1 .708-.708l3 3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .708l-3 3a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L10.293 8.5H4.5A.5.5 0 0 1 4 